sam_chang: heads-up: noticed a weird gap in traces when we switch apps to structured logging (JSON). request-id sometimes disappears after an auth retry and logs end up with a `request_id` key = null. :thinking:

tess_devx: structured logs should help, not hurt. is this during retry or all flows? any quick repro?

sam_chang: only during the OAuth refresh retry. initial incoming request has `X-Request-ID` header and we also write it into OTEL baggage as `request_id`. after refresh, the outgoing retry request headers show the id, but downstream logs (which ingest JSON) show `request_id: null`.

rohan_obs: can you paste the JSON log lines (sanitized)? small ones please.

sam_chang: sure, sanitized:
```
{"ts":"2026-03-26T14:01:05Z","level":"info","msg":"auth recv","headers":{"authorization":"Bearer ***","x-request-id":"rid-428"},"baggage":{"request_id":"rid-428"}}
{"ts":"2026-03-26T14:01:06Z","level":"warn","msg":"refresh start"}
{"ts":"2026-03-26T14:01:07Z","level":"debug","msg":"outgoing retry","headers":{"authorization":"Bearer ***"},"baggage":{}}
{"ts":"2026-03-26T14:01:08Z","level":"info","msg":"downstream handled","request_id":null}
```

abby_sre: interesting: two things jump out: 1) baggage is emptied on retry line; 2) downstream `request_id` field got set to null, maybe because the log enrichment pipeline merges header->baggage and overwrote the key with an empty value.

rohan_obs: exactly. our log-enricher merges HTTP headers and OTEL baggage into a single structured context before indexing. if the retry request came with headers but the app's log line didn't include baggage (empty obj), enrichment merged baggage (empty) over headers, resulting in `request_id:null`. merging rules are last-write-wins. bug.

sam_chang: so two root causes: a) context propagation lost baggage when the retry executed in a separate execution context; b) enrichment merge order is brittle and overwrites header-derived keys with empty baggage. both need fixes.

tess_devx: quick mitigations: 1) ensure retry path preserves baggage by copying it into the retry request headers (add to SDK templates); 2) make the log-enricher prefer header values when baggage is empty or absent rather than blindly overwriting; and 3) add a sanity check in structured logging to avoid emitting empty baggage objects.

rohan_obs: agreed. I'll change the enricher merge to 'prefer non-empty values' and add a unit test where baggage is {} and headers contain x-request-id -> final event keeps the header value. also add an alert if `request_id` becomes null in ingestion for more than 1% of auth-refresh flows.

abby_sre: sampleapp-side, add a small opt-in middleware that does: if (ctx.baggage.request_id) attach header `x-request-id` to outgoing retry requests; if not, read `x-request-id` header and set baggage before retry. that covers both baggage-first and header-first apps. put it in Node and Python templates and a small helper in Go/Java/.NET.

sam_chang: will open a small PR to the Node sampleapp that adds axios interceptor + log enrichment sanity checks. snippet for Node interceptor: ```js
axios.interceptors.request.use(cfg => {
  const rid = baggage.get('request_id') || logging.getHeader('x-request-id');
  if (rid) { cfg.headers['x-request-id'] = rid; baggage.set('request_id', rid); }
  return cfg;
});
```

rohan_obs: thanks. I'll also update the enricher config and add tests. one more item: the redactor currently runs after enrichment and will collapse header maps if it sees Authorization. that can transform `headers` into a single string then enrichment parsing fails. we should redraft the pipeline: parse structured headers early, redact per-key, then enrich. avoid collapsing maps into strings.

redact-bot: note: redaction rule DX-HEAD-99 triggers when Authorization present. current behavior: replace 'headers' value with 'HEADERS_REDACTED'. Proposed change: iterate keys and set Authorization -> 'REDACTED' leaving other keys intact. Filing infra ticket #INF-834.

abby_sre: excellent. action plan: 1) rohan update enricher merge semantics + add alert; 2) infra change redactor to per-key mask (no collapsing) + tests; 3) devex add sdk parity doc 'Retry-aware baggage/header propagation' with Node/Python/Go/Java/.NET snippets; 4) sampleapp patches to inject baggage->header on retry and to avoid emitting empty baggage objects. add integration test in telemetry CI that runs oauth-refresh and asserts final indexed event has non-null request_id.

tess_devx: tiny doc note: recommend apps populate both header AND OTEL baggage for request id on inbound so downstream libs can pick whichever they prefer. that prevents single-point failures.

sam_chang: i'll open PRs and paste links. short staging workaround: set env var `LOG_ENRICHER_PREFER_HEADERS=true` to flip merge order until patches land. :memo:

rohan_obs: deploying redaction patch to staging env for smoke tests. monitoring ingestion alerts.

